calleb a coder at the world's largest  Internet company wins a competition to  spend a week at the mountain retreat of  his reclusive billionaire boss Nathan he  cannot believe his look and he's even  more surprised to find out he's there to  interact with a female robot called Ava  created by Nathan and to find out  whether she's truly self-aware like a  human being as I walked into the cinema  to watch ex machina my expectations were  sky-high first of all because of the  trio of uber talented actors who star in  the film  that's Alyssa vikander Oscar Isaac and  domhnall gleeson and second because  writer Alex Garland has pretty much  nailed every script he's written from 28  days later to Dredd speaking of which I  would love to see a Dredd sequel so  sadly it looks like that ain't gonna  happen anyway  how could ex machina possibly live up to  my level of anticipation well not only  did it live up to it but it actually  exceeded it as well as writing ex  machina Alex Carla makes his debut in  the director's chair and he excels in  both departments the script is clever  and coherent while the visuals are  simply stunning because so much of ex  machina is about calleb Nathan and Ava  getting to know each other most of the  film revolves around conversations  between them rather than action in the  hands of Garland's this isn't a problem  though as he's written a dialogue driven  script that's full of tension deals with  big issues in a clear manner and is  consistently fascinating in fact I was  gripped from the start right through to  the end by Garland's perfect blend of  intelligent sci-fi and psychological  thriller infused with horror and he's  also managed to inject a good dose of  humor into the film too sometimes in the  most unlikely moments and this works  just wonderfully look at in particular  for one of the best dance scenes I've  seen in a very long time he's also sewn  with a crack team of on-screen and  behind-the-scenes talent who really make  the film pop if you've watched my review  of the wartime drama testament of youth  you'll know how highly I think of  Swedish actress Alyssa vikander and you  can click here to watch that video and  she's just as dazzling again in ex  machina giving another finely honed  performance as female robot Ava vikander  speech facial expressions gestures in  gate all combined  beautifully to suggest an other nurse  intermingled with humanity and you can  sense vikander's early training as a  ballerina in the way she's able to  completely control her body brilliantly  blurring the line between how humans and  robots move Oscar Isaac brings Nathan to  life  oh so superbly which is hardly  surprising given his past performances  in films like drive inside Llewyn Davis  and a most violent year he's one of  those actors who can totally vanish into  a roll and he does so to great effect in  ex machina Isaac cleverly balances his  performance on a knife edge between what  Nathan is like on the surface and what  he's like underneath so despite Nathan's  super-chill demeanor and his apparent  air of down-to-earth mate eNOS there's  more than a trace of the supreme control  freak about him between his superb turn  in ex machina  and roles coming up in star wars and  x-men apocalypse the next 18 months are  going to be huge for Isaac just like  Isaac and vikander domhnall gleeson star  is very much on the rise this year with  episode 7 among a number of films to see  him in in 2015  Gleason's worked before with both  vikander and Alex garland on Joe  Wright's adaptation of Anna Karenina and  on the sci-fi action movie Dredd and he  impresses yet again in ex machina with  an intelligent and natural performance  as the softly spoken Caleb oh and if you  want to find out more about what the  year ahead holds for Oscar Isaac  domhnall gleeson and Alyssa vikander  click here to watch my video on the top  10 actors you must watch in 2015 much  deserved props also go to  cinematographer Rob Hardy and this is  actually his first sci-fi movie he's  worked on he did an exceptional job on  testament of youth and his work on ex  machina is outstanding comic book asked  its jock who did the early concept  design for Ava and the movies visual  effects team have also done an AB C's  stellar job bringing Ava to life and I  must also mention production designer  Marc Digby and set decorator  Michelle day whose work is so crucial to  the whole eerily beautiful feel of the  film outside Nathan's home can research  facility there are acres of gorgeous  wilderness full with mountains trees and  waterfalls but the building's  geographical isolation coupled with the  fact that callebs more or less confined  there gives the whole film a decidedly  austra phobic atmosphere after that the  building sleek lines and toned down  modernist feel and the whole space feels  strangely unsettling to sum up ex  machina is a superlative sci-fi flick  that benefits from an outstanding script  pitch perfect performances and stunning  visuals what's not to like ex machina  gets 5 out of 5 flicks so what did you  think of ex machina and what's your  favorite robot movie + how would you  react to a world of sentient robots let  me know in the comments below and if you  liked this video hit the thumbs-up  button and subscribe for my weekly movie  reviews and interviews  thanks for watching and see you next  time yippee-ki-yay movie lovers  you
 

